  "notes" : [
    "Keys are the RFC 8032 section 7.1 TEST 1, TEST 2 and TEST 3 Ed25519 keys: published test constants that must never sign anything real.",
    "Ed25519 is deterministic, so every signature below is reproducible from the key and the preimage.",
    "One preimage rule, for every type: a record is verified against magic || the 32 challenge bytes || the canonical bytes. The magic is the signature domain, the accountId is inside the canonical bytes, and the challenge is inside every signature.",
    "The challenge below is the 32 bytes 00..1f. A real challenge is CSPRNG, minted once, held against one account and one stepped-up session, and burned on acceptance and on refusal.",
    "seq and prevHash are the chain positions these records would occupy: the grant follows the adoption, the revocation follows the grant, and either recovery replaces the grant at seq 2. GUAO Oppose takes no slot, so it carries the seq and prevHash of the record it cancels.",
    "A conforming implementation reproduces every canonicalHex, sha256Hex, preimageSha256Hex and signatureB64, and refuses every entry under rejections with the reason named there."
  ],
